
# SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION (SRS)

## NIMR INTEGRATED NCD MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

**System Name:** NIMR Integrated NCD Management System
**Host Organization:** National Institute for Medical Research (NIMR)
**Country:** United Republic of Tanzania
**System Type:** Clinical NCD Management and Monitoring Platform
**Initial NCDs:** Diabetes, Cardiovascular/Cardiac Diseases, Sickle Cell Disease
**Architecture:** Modular Monolith, extensible toward Microservices
**Primary Users:** NIMR, participating hospitals/facilities, clinicians, NCD coordinators, laboratory staff, pharmacy staff, data managers and authorized administrators
**Version:** 1.0

---

# 1. INTRODUCTION

## 1.1 Purpose

The NIMR Integrated NCD Management System is a centralized platform for managing Non-Communicable Disease services across participating hospitals and health facilities in Tanzania.

The system will support the complete patient lifecycle from registration and screening through clinical assessment, diagnosis, treatment, follow-up, monitoring and outcomes.

The platform will initially support:

1. Diabetes
2. Cardiovascular/Cardiac Diseases
3. Sickle Cell Disease

The system shall be designed so that additional NCDs can be introduced without redesigning the core platform.

Potential future diseases include:

* Hypertension
* Chronic Kidney Disease
* Cancer
* Asthma
* Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease
* Epilepsy
* Other chronic conditions

---

# 2. SYSTEM OWNERSHIP AND HOSTING

The system will be hosted and managed under the **National Institute for Medical Research (NIMR)**.

NIMR will be the principal system owner and platform administrator.

Hospitals and health facilities will participate as service-delivery facilities within the NIMR-hosted platform.

There is therefore no requirement for a generic multi-organization hierarchy.

The system will instead use:

```text
NIMR
 │
 └── Tanzania
      │
      └── NIMR Operational Zone
           │
           └── Region
                │
                └── District
                     │
                     └── Hospital / Facility
```

The geographical structure shall support reporting and access control.

---

# 3. SYSTEM OBJECTIVES

The system shall:

1. Digitize NCD screening and management.
2. Provide a centralized longitudinal patient record.
3. Support multiple NCD conditions for one patient.
4. Standardize NCD clinical workflows.
5. Support laboratory investigations.
6. Support ECG services.
7. Support echocardiography.
8. Support radiology/imaging.
9. Support pharmacy and medication management.
10. Support enterprise-wide inventory management.
11. Support scheduled and unscheduled patient encounters.
12. Provide configurable follow-up scheduling.
13. Support automatic, manual and hybrid scheduling.
14. Support disease-specific protocols.
15. Provide facility-to-national reporting.
16. Provide disease-specific reporting.
17. Enforce geographical access restrictions.
18. Enforce disease and module access restrictions.
19. Maintain comprehensive audit trails.
20. Support future NCD expansion.

