# 83. CORE DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The NIMR Integrated NCD Management System shall be:

**One NIMR-hosted NCD platform with one shared patient and clinical core, configurable disease-specific workflows, reusable clinical service modules, an automated follow-up engine, and hierarchical access control from facility to national level.**

The architecture deliberately avoids:

* Generic multi-organization tenancy
* Separate study-level access
* Separate laboratory systems per disease
* Separate ECG systems per disease
* Separate pharmacy systems per disease
* Hardcoded disease-specific core architectures

Instead, the system uses:

**NIMR → Geography/Facilities → Patients → Encounters → NCD Programs → Clinical Services → Follow-up → Outcomes → Reporting**

with access controlled through:

**Role + Geography/Facility + Disease + Module + Action.**
